WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back!
-Great to be back.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:04.637
-It's so happy to have you here.
And this is such a --

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.438 line:92%
this is such a cool show.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a show where you talk
about your father.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.709
-Mm-hmm.
-And you tell stories about him.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.046
You also read stories that he
read to you when you were a kid

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:16.082
and then in turn when he
was older, you read to him.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-So this is

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.952 size:78% position:39%
a very personal show,
a very intimate show?

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, but the stories are
fantastic stories, and I begin

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:27.627
reading them, but then I perform
the hell out of them.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Uh-huh.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.131
-I pretty much do everything
I can possibly do as an actor.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's a fantastic way
to spend a couple hours,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.670
but you, again, because this is
more personal, obviously,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.239 size:75% position:38%
you've been on stage
a lot on Broadway.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.641
You're going to have people who
are talking during shows.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ] Oh, yes.
You -- and you recently had

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
an issue where you had to stop
the show?

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:49.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yesterday, your producer
was in the audience.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It wasn't him.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:55.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank God. [ Laughs ]
-I walked out to a very nice

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.856 line:92%
entrance applause like that.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
As soon as the applause
died down,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
I haven't even begun yet,
right in front of me

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:04.364
in the first row center,
there was a fellow talking

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
just about as loud as we're
talking right now.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-"I don't want to go

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Sardi's again.
I always go to Sar--"

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like... [ Stammers ]
And he kept on talking.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was talking,
and he was talking.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And all I could think was,

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I have two hours to go."
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I -- all I could do was
say, "is there anything

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can do to help here?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.588 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"Is there a problem?

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.925
Because only one of us can talk,
you know."

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.495
And the audience was on my side.
-I bet. I would imagine.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I would imagine.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:38.565 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So anyways, it was pretty...
-No one said,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
"let him talk, John!"
-No. [ Laughs ]

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.437
-"He's got to figure out a meal
after this!"

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] That's right.
-You've obviously had

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
that happen over the years
being on stage a lot.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:53.313
You have sort of a heroic --
I mean, obviously it was very

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
heroic for the people
in the audience last night.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But you went above

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
and beyond one time.
-There was -- actually it was

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:01.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
quite a beautiful moment.
I was in this wonderful play,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:05.825
"M. Butterfly" in the late '80s
in which I played --

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
I constantly talked directly
to the audience.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.697 line:92%
I went in and out of scenes.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there was a scene where
a dance was going on.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.071
I was simply watching it.
And I noticed a woman,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
an old woman, again,
in the front row center.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.609
That seems to be the key seat...
-Yeah.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...in all my stories.
-Say the ushers go, "you look

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:27.213
like -- you look like trouble.
Let me put you in the front."

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:32.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was struggling to her feet
and trying --

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.087 line:92%
She must have been in her 80s.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trying to make her way
to the aisle.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as soon as
the dance started,

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I began to talk
to the audience again,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
she was still standing there.
I said, "can I help you?

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there something wrong?"
Once again.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had to be brought
to the aisle

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
laying down on her back.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The EMTs came in to take care
of her.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:58.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
The audience went completely
silent.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:01.814
Word got to the house manager,
to the stage manager, to me,

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she was all right.
I told the crowd.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
They started to applaud.
I said, "quiet down."

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.487 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must have taken about
five minutes.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And they -- she was, indeed,

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:16.229
all right, but, you know,
as years have gone by,

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.230 line:92%
like a dozen people have told me

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were in the audience
that night,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:22.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they'd never seen anything
more theatrical.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-But then is it true that you

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:28.541
also ran into her son? Is it --
-Oh, yes.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't run into him.
I was doing a Q&amp;A

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Museum of Broadcasting.
TV and Broadcasting

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:36.883
and doing -- answering questions
from the audience.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:40.520
A gentleman got up, without a
question, but he had a letter.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.287 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he read it out loud.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:45.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a letter from me
to this old woman.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience "Aw"s ]
Years before saying,

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:50.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm so sorry you missed
the rest of the show.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:54.634
Please come back as my guest
and come have tea with me."

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:58.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he told the audience
that I had done this.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-And I didn't remember.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.041 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, I was like...

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:08.448 size:75% position:38%
All I could say was,
"what a nice guy."

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

